000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/49351177/2026-michigan-warde-manuel-athletic-department-tenure-line-investigation","type":"Story","byline":"Paolo Uggetti","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"What are the conference title game clinching scenarios in Week 13?","description":"Plenty of spots are still up for grabs entering the final week of the regular season.","published":"2026-11-24T18:22:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50583399/conference-title-game-clinching-scenarios-week-13","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Trev Alberts told he won't be Michigan AD after agreement","description":"Trev Alberts was \"shocked and disheartened\" to be informed by the search firm representing Michigan that he will not be the Wolverines' next AD, he told ESPN.","published":"2026-11-24T23:50:56.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50583155/attorney-trev-alberts-told-next-ad-michigan","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Pete Thamel and Dan Wetzel","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4875126/horace-lockett","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Horace_Lockett"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Horace Lockett","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Horace_Lockett","description":"American football player (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:38:20Z","intro":"Horace Lockett (born July 26, 2004) is an American college football defensive tackle for the UCF Knights. He previously played for the Georgia Tech Yellow Jackets.","sections":[{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As a true freshman at Georgia Tech in 2022, Lockett made three appearances. He saw more playing time in the 2023 season and tallied 25 tackles along with 2.5 tackles-for-loss (TFLs) and a forced fumble. However, a hand injury resulted in Lockett being kept out of every game during the 2024 season. The following year, he transferred to the UCF Knights. With UCF, Lockett won a starting role and posted 13 tackles, three TFLs, a sack and two pass breakups. However, a pectoral injury ended his season after four games. Lockett returned for a final season with the Knights in 2026."}]}}